# NyxOS server package set: the same vanilla Arch base + BlackArch
# privacy/anonymity tool groups + Nyx control-layer daemons as
# packages.x86_64, minus every package that exists only to put a GUI on the
# screen. Every Nyx daemon (kill switch, VPN, DNS enforcement, identity
# randomization, device control, integrity verification, telemetry,
# diagnostics) is a systemd service with a Unix-socket control plane and
# neither needs nor references a display — nyx-workflow and
# nyx-diagnostics already give this profile full CLI access to everything
# the desktop dashboard exposes. One package name per line, '#' starts a
# comment.

# --- Base system ---
base
base-devel
linux
linux-firmware
linux-headers
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
sudo
which
vim
nano
git
man-db
man-pages
bash-completion
reflector

# --- Boot / install tooling ---
syslinux
grub
efibootmgr
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
gptfdisk
parted
cryptsetup
arch-install-scripts
archinstall
rsync

# --- Networking core ---
networkmanager
network-manager-applet
nftables
openssh
wireguard-tools
openvpn
xray
shadowsocks-rust
badvpn
iproute2
iputils
traceroute
curl

# --- Privacy stack (control layer targets) ---
tor
dnscrypt-proxy

# --- BlackArch signing keys, so the live medium's pacman-init.service can
# `pacman-key --populate blackarch` and verify [blackarch] packages (the
# NyxOS key comes from the nyxos keyring staged by iso/build.sh). ---
blackarch-keyring

# --- Second anonymity network, alongside Tor. Headless-friendly (i2pd is a
# routing daemon, no GUI needed); not enabled by default, same reasoning as
# the desktop profile. ---
i2pd

# --- Encrypted-container volumes; veracrypt's CLI mode works headless. ---
veracrypt

# --- NyxOS control layer (built from install/pkgbuild/, see build.sh) ---
# nyx-thunar-integration, nyx-desktop-sessions and nyx-dashboard are dropped
# here: the first two only exist to integrate with Thunar/LightDM, which
# this profile doesn't install, and the dashboard is a GTK application with
# nothing to render on a headless box. Every other daemon/CLI is plain
# systemd + a Unix socket and is fully controllable headless.
nyx-health
nyx-vpn
nyx-identity
nyx-devices
nyx-telemetry
nyx-diagnostics
nyx-dns
nyx-integrity
nyx-wipe
nyx-isolation
nyx-workflow
nyx-hardening
nyx-watch

# --- Mandatory access control (AppArmor) — not GUI-dependent. The kernel
# lsm= boot parameter and the apparmor.service enable-symlink are baked
# into the shared boot configs/airootfs, so this package must be present
# here too or that already-enabled service fails to start. ---
apparmor

# --- Rust toolchain for the control layer ---
# Still needed even on this profile: the Nyx packages above are built from
# source at ISO-build time regardless of which profile is selected.
rust

# --- Interactive shell: zsh plus the two plugins. The desktop profile's
# /etc/zsh/zshrc (nyx-desktop-sessions, GUI-only, not on this profile)
# wires them up; here they are available to a user's own ~/.zshrc. ---
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting

# --- BlackArch/extra: networking, sniffing, spoofing, proxying, crypto
# attack, and disk forensics essentials. Named individual tools, not the
# blackarch-networking/sniffer/spoof/proxy/crypto/forensic/anti-forensic
# groups (each pulls in hundreds of packages) — same "named tools, not whole
# groups" reasoning as the wireless/blue-team section below, applied
# consistently here instead of contradicting it. Matches how Kali's own
# default/live toolset is curated, not a full category dump. Anti-forensic
# needs are already covered by wipe/secure-delete/gocryptfs/veracrypt/mat2
# above, so no separate package is added for that category. All seven of
# these are in Arch's own official repos (core/extra), no BlackArch
# dependency needed. Headless profile: wireshark-qt swapped for
# wireshark-cli (tshark) — no GUI on this profile. ---
nmap
wireshark-cli
macchanger
proxychains-ng
hashcat
sleuthkit
binwalk

# --- Wireless/Bluetooth/malware-analysis essentials (audited against
# Kali's own tool metapackages 2026-09-18 — Kodachi has no equivalent for
# these at all). Named individual tools, not whole blackarch-<category>
# groups (a normal Kali or Kodachi install doesn't ship a category's full
# tool set by default either) — these six are all in Arch's own official
# `extra` repo, no BlackArch dependency needed for this part at all.
aircrack-ng
kismet
wifite
reaver
bettercap
yara

# --- SDR + blue-team/defensive tooling: individual BlackArch packages,
# same "named tools, not whole groups" reasoning as above. Kodachi has no
# defensive-security angle at all, so this is a real differentiator rather
# than catch-up. A security appliance benefits from this tooling with or
# without a GUI. ---
gqrx-scanner
rtl-433
chkrootkit
suricata
zeek

# --- Application isolation (backs nyx-isolation) ---
firejail
firetools
podman

# --- Desktop security/privacy apps, wired into Thunar/nyx-wipe/nyx-isolation ---
keepassxc
mat2
perl-image-exiftool
wipe
gocryptfs
usbguard
xterm
ent
gnupg
xclip
ethtool
usbutils
secure-delete
